 "text": "Hello, how are things going? It depends which one. Dutch is much closer with more similar vocabulary. Norwegian is harder with lots of surprising oddities. In Norwegian you say a before the Vowel in the word you' addressing someone with, like av and er. Dutch just uses het. It can take you by surprise the first few times. The short vowels are different, and some consonants like the p in pitt sound different. The e in to be is pronounced like e in the. Read Norwegian for beginners is much simpler. And Duolingo has Dutch and both Nordic languages. Go with what you choose to practice with a friend. That makes bigger difference than the original language.",
